+## big-pickle — pass 2
+
+The tether everyone found in pass 1 named the right GOAL but the wrong mechanism. GM-A serves it at zero action cost: the aura stops being positional luck when the orbit swarm IS the drain's physical form — no forced-move roll, replaced by real decisions (flank him, push him out of orbit, bait a fling). This solves the weakness I flagged better than my own drag did. GM-B is the same goal riskier: a 13-HP front-liner on Ebonyflesh and Avoid Death is strictly more fragile, and its sweep niche punishes anchor campers — meta, less mirror. GM-A also subsumes my First Splinter's material (anchor glass, Magic-scaled), so the swap is honest. Strongest case against GM-A — the floated "catch-spells wall" is unspecified and could collide with the Atronach Stone's negate, reskinning the Bound Bow — fails because the Unmaking gift keys off Jasper's own negate, so the wall is dressing, and the open stats (Magic roll, damage under 12, Free recall, Bonus hurl after a negate) are numbers First Splinter already validated. Adopt GM-A with those stats.
+
+VERDICT: SIGN v2 + GM-A (Magic roll, dmg<12, Free recall, Bonus hurl on negate)

